# 50. TESTING STRATEGY

Use pytest.

Create tests for:

## Attendance

```text
check-in success
check-in duplicate
check-out success
check-out without check-in
double checkout
overnight shift
late arrival
early exit
grace period
work duration
break duration
```

## Shift

```text
create
update
delete/archive
duplicate code
overnight shift
invalid time
```

## Tenant Security

Test:

```text
Tenant A cannot access Tenant B attendance.
Tenant A cannot access Tenant B shift.
Tenant A cannot assign Tenant B shift.
Tenant A cannot modify Tenant B employee attendance.
```

## RBAC

Test:

```text
Employee
Manager
HR
Admin
Super Admin
```

with appropriate permission boundaries.

---

# 51. PROPERTY / EDGE CASE TESTING

Test important boundary conditions.

Examples:

```text
Check-in exactly at shift start
Check-in exactly at grace boundary
Check-in one minute after grace
Checkout exactly at shift end
Checkout one minute before end
Checkout one minute after end
Midnight crossing
Month boundary
Year boundary
Leap year
Holiday
Weekly off
Inactive employee
Terminated employee
```

---

# 52. TIMEZONE TESTING

Test multiple timezones.

At minimum:

```text
Asia/Kolkata
UTC
America/New_York
Europe/London
Asia/Singapore
```

Verify attendance dates and shift calculations.

---

# 53. DATABASE TESTING

Verify:

* migrations
* foreign keys
* unique constraints
* tenant isolation
* transaction rollback
* concurrent check-in protection
* historical shift assignments

---

# 54. PERFORMANCE TESTING

Test with realistic datasets.

Example:

```text
10,000 employees
1 year attendance
multiple shifts
multiple branches
```

Verify:

* attendance list performance
* employee attendance history
* dashboard aggregation
* date filtering
* pagination
* shift resolution

Avoid N+1 queries.

---

# 55. SECURITY TESTING

Test for:

```text
IDOR
Cross-tenant access
Privilege escalation
Unauthorized attendance modification
Employee impersonation
Parameter tampering
Mass assignment
```

Example:

A user must not be able to modify:

```json
{
  "employee_id": "another_employee"
}
```

to manipulate another employee's attendance.

---

# 56. MASS ASSIGNMENT PROTECTION

Do not blindly accept database fields from request payloads.

For example, clients must not be able to directly set:

```text
tenant_id
created_by
updated_by
approval_status
approved_by
```

unless explicitly allowed through controlled workflows.

---

# 57. DATABASE TRANSACTIONS

Check-in/out operations should be transactional.

Conceptually:

```text
BEGIN
 |
 +-- Resolve employee
 |
 +-- Resolve shift
 |
 +-- Validate state
 |
 +-- Create event
 |
 +-- Update attendance
 |
 +-- Audit
 |
COMMIT
```

If any critical operation fails:

```text
ROLLBACK
```

---

# 58. NOTIFICATION FOUNDATION

Prepare event hooks for future notifications.

Example:

```text
Employee checked in
Employee checked out
Late arrival
Missed checkout
Regularization approved
```

Do not build the complete notification system in Phase 4.

Create clean integration points.

